## Control {{controlId}}: Screen Individuals Prior to Authorizing Access to Systems Containing CUI

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization screens individuals prior to authorizing CUI access within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through background investigation procedures documented in "Personnel Security Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.humanResourcesManager}}.

All personnel requiring access to CUI undergo appropriate background investigations prior to access authorization:

**Screening Requirements:**
- **Employees:** Tier 1 (NACI-equivalent) background investigation completed through Defense Counterintelligence and Security Agency (DCSA) prior to CUI access provisioning
- **Contractors:** Background investigation appropriate to contract requirements and CUI sensitivity level
- **Temporary Personnel:** Escort-only access until screening is completed and adjudicated
- **Re-investigation:** Personnel re-screened every 5 years or upon promotion to positions with elevated CUI access

**Access Authorization Process:**
- HR confirms favorable screening adjudication before notifying {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}
- Account provisioned in Entra ID only after screening verification documented
- CUI group membership granted after screening confirmation and role-based need-to-know verification

{{#if cuiGroupExists}}
**CUI Access Population:**
The "{{groupDisplayName}}" security group ({{memberCount}} members) contains only personnel with verified screening status.
{{/if}}

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Screen all personnel before CUI access; maintain screening status records; initiate re-investigations per schedule
- **Frequency:** Prior to access authorization; re-investigation every 5 years
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.humanResourcesManager}}
- **Documentation:** Personnel Security Policy v1.0, DCSA investigation records, adjudication memoranda

**Review Frequency:** Annually by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine personnel security files, screening completion records, adjudication documentation, and CUI group membership against screening status.

